5. Explain what a web server is and give examples of commonly used servers.

A web server is software that receives requests from users' browsers and sends back web pages or other resources. It acts as a bridge between the client and the website.

Some commonly used web servers are:

Apache HTTP Server
Nginx
Microsoft IIS
Node.js with Express
6. Define the roles of a frontend developer, backend developer, and database administrator in a project.

A Frontend Developer creates the user interface and ensures that the website is responsive and easy to use.

A Backend Developer develops the server-side logic, manages APIs, handles authentication, and connects the application with the database.

A Database Administrator (DBA) manages the database, ensures data security, performs backups, and improves database performance.

