8. Explain the difference between static and dynamic websites. Provide an example of each.

A static website displays the same content to every visitor. Its content does not change unless the developer updates the files manually.

Example: Personal portfolio website.

A dynamic website generates content based on user input or data stored in a database. Different users may see different content.

Example: Facebook, Amazon, or Gmail.

9. Research and list five web browsers. Explain how rendering engines differ between them.

Some popular web browsers are:

Google Chrome
Mozilla Firefox
Microsoft Edge
Apple Safari
Opera

These browsers use different rendering engines to display web pages.

Chrome – Blink
Edge – Blink
Firefox – Gecko
Safari – WebKit
Opera – Blink

A rendering engine converts HTML, CSS, and JavaScript into the webpage that users see. Different rendering engines may render certain features differently and have different performance levels. 

